This grant is limited to the material you actually submit for inclusion and to
use within this project. It transfers no ownership: you keep the copyright in
your contribution, as set out in Section 5. The copyright holder is under no
obligation to accept, merge or keep any contribution.

You confirm that you are entitled to grant this right for the material you
submit and that it does not infringe the rights of others.

### Ideas, bug reports and suggestions

An issue, a bug report, a feature request or a suggestion made in conversation
is **not** a code contribution and is not covered by the grant above. No rights
in it pass to the copyright holder.

The copyright holder may nevertheless act on such a report or suggestion,
including by implementing it independently, without owing you anything in
return. Equally, making a report or a suggestion gives you no rights in this
project and no claim to authorship of it.

If you include code in an issue or a message and offer it for inclusion, that
code counts as a code contribution under this Section.

## 11. Termination

The permissions granted in Section 1 terminate automatically if you fail to
comply with any term of this license.

### Curing a violation

Curing a violation means ending the violating conduct and undoing its effect.
Depending on what went wrong, that is:

- Adding or correcting the credit and the repository link required by Section 2.
- Taking down a download that Section 1 or Section 4 does not permit.
- Restoring this license, in full and unchanged, where it was replaced, altered
  or removed.
- Removing the price, paywall or payment requirement placed on the software.

### Reinstatement

Your permissions are reinstated:

- **provisionally**, as soon as you end the violation, and **permanently** if
  the copyright holder does not notify you of that violation within 60 days
  after it ended;
- **permanently**, if the copyright holder notifies you of the violation and you
  cure it within 30 days of receiving that notice;
- **permanently**, if the copyright holder reinstates them expressly in writing.

Reinstatement under the first two points is not available if the copyright
holder has already notified you of the same violation once before and you have
repeated it. In that case only an express written reinstatement restores your
permissions.

Notice may be given in writing by any means by which the copyright holder can
reasonably reach you, including a message on the platform where you published
your version.

Reinstatement does not affect any claim arising from the period during which the
violation lasted.

The termination of your permissions does not terminate the permissions of anyone
who received a copy from you in compliance with this license.

Sections 5, 6, 9 and 10 survive the termination of this license.

